%N A279260 Numbers which are cyclops palindromic in their binary reflected Gray code representation.
%C A279260 Cyclops palindromic numbers in base 2 are numbers with middle bit 0, having equal number of 1's on both side of the 0. There is a single 0 bit in the middle and the total number of bits is odd. The middle '0' represents the eye of a cyclops.
%C A279260 a(n) mod 6 = 0.
%C A279260 In the linked Equilateral Completion paper, C(m) is the number of equilateral triangles of order m containing the identity floretion base word e_m as a vertex. Proposition 4.6 gives C(m) = (4^m + (-2)^m - 2)/3, so a(n) = C(n+1). All such triangles are nonlocal by Corollary 5.11. - _Creighton Dement_, Oct 15 2026
%H A279260 Indranil Ghosh, <a href="/A279260/b279260.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A279260 Creighton Dement, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.15925">Equilateral Completion in Floretion Triangular Coordinates: Locality, Product Points, and Reflection Symmetry</a>, arXiv:2608.15925 [math.CO], 2026. See Proposition 4.6, Corollary 5.11, Section 10, and Appendix A.
%H A279260 Creighton Dement, <a href="/A279260/a279260_1.txt">Floretion coefficient identities for A279260 (proof and related sequences)</a>, Oct 2026.
%H A279260 Creighton Dement, <a href="https://www.floretions.com">Online Floretion Calculator</a>; see also the OEIS tab.
%H A279260 Indranil Ghosh, <a href="/A279260/a279260.txt">Proof of 6|{(-2*(1+((-2)^n)-(2^(2*n+1))))/3}</a>.
%H A279260 Brady Haran and Simon Pampena, <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HPfAnX5blO0">Glitch Primes and Cyclops Numbers</a>, Numberphile video, (2015).
%H A279260 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (3,6,-8).
%F A279260 a(n) = (-2*(1+((-2)^n)-(2^(2*n+1))))/3.
%F A279260 From _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 28 2025: (Start)
%F A279260 a(n) = 6*A084175(n).
%F A279260 G.f.: 6*x/((1 - x)*(1 + 2*x)*(1 - 4*x)). (End)
%F A279260 E.g.f.: 2*(2*exp(4*x) - exp(x) - exp(-2*x))/3. - _Stefano Spezia_, Oct 28 2025
%e A279260 90 is in the sequence because the binary reflected Gray code representation of 90 is '1110111' which is a cyclops palindromic binary number.
%t A279260 A279260[n_] := -2*(1 + (-2)^n - 2^(2*n+1))/3; Array[A279260, 30, 0] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Feb 04 2026 *)
%t A279260 (* Alternative: *)
%t A279260 LinearRecurrence[{3, 6, -8}, {0, 6, 18}, 30] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Feb 04 2026 *)
%o A279260 (Python)
%o A279260 def a(n):
%o A279260     return (-2*(1+((-2)**n)-(2**(2*n+1))))/3
%o A279260 (PARI) a(n)=(-2*(1+((-2)^n)-(2^(2*n+1))))/3 \\ _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Jun 29 2018
